(7233269, 1118172, 60173, '<td valign="top">Those crazy spikes are my husband''s worst nightmare! I think it''s wicked cool though.  :)</td>', 'Those crazy spikes are my husband''s worst nightmare! I think it''s wicked cool though.  :)', '2014-06-25 15:06:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(7233272, 1117961, 60173, '<td valign="top">These images always crack me up, because they look like they''re going so fast, but then you look at the speed gauge and they''re not going nearly that fast. You''re barely moving, lol. Really nice job on this.<br/> <br/></td>', 'These images always crack me up, because they look like they''re going so fast, but then you look at the speed gauge and they''re not going nearly that fast. You''re barely moving, lol. Really nice job on this. ', '2014-06-25 15:10:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(7233276, 1118245, 60173, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by littlemav:</b></div><hr/><i> U should get many extra points for keeping a cat still for 10 seconds!   I do really like this! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>That''s exactly what I was thinking. Is it even possible to get a cat to hold still this long? Sure he looks pretty content in with his little blanket, but still. My cat constantly turns his head when I want his picture.</td>', 'Originally posted by littlemav: U should get many extra points for keeping a cat still for 10 seconds!   I do really like this!   That''s exactly what I was thinking. Is it even possible to get a cat to hold still this long? Sure he looks pretty content in with his little blanket, but still. My cat constantly turns his head when I want his picture.', '2014-06-25 15:15:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(7233278, 1118015, 60173, '<td valign="top">I so miss the fireflies from when I lived in Indiana. Such amazing little creatures. I will admit, I was always very confused by my amusement when they''d splat on my windshield. It''s so neat watching their glow streak up the window, yet so sad that you''ve just ended their precious little life.<br/> <br/>You''ve done a pretty good job capturing their glow. I wouldn''t have thought it would really show up, but I guess 10 seconds is the trick.</td>', 'I so miss the fireflies from when I lived in Indiana. Such amazing little creatures. I will admit, I was always very confused by my amusement when they''d splat on my windshield. It''s so neat watching their glow streak up the window, yet so sad that you''ve just ended their precious little life. You''ve done a pretty good job capturing their glow. I wouldn''t have thought it would really show up, but I guess 10 seconds is the trick.', '2014-06-25 15:18:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(7233282, 1118052, 60173, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by littlemav:</b></div><hr/><i> I LOVED this, it should be wayyyy up towards the top. Try to make you pix larger next time  I size my final at 800 pix on the high side, and then save for web in Photoshop, if you don''t have PS do that size and then take the res to 72. That should keep your shot large and get under the 300 mg allowance for DPC .  I think that''s the ONLY reason this is placed so low. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I agree, this was worth more than it received, but it''s strictly because the image is so small. I''ve noticed your other entries have also been under the 800px max. In addition to <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=117534" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">littlemav</a>''s advice, here''s a tutorial that may help.<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=26" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Using Photoshop to Prepare Photos for DPC Challenges</a></td>', 'Originally posted by littlemav: I LOVED this, it should be wayyyy up towards the top. Try to make you pix larger next time  I size my final at 800 pix on the high side, and then save for web in Photoshop, if you don''t have PS do that size and then take the res to 72. That should keep your shot large and get under the 300 mg allowance for DPC .  I think that''s the ONLY reason this is placed so low.   I agree, this was worth more than it received, but it''s strictly because the image is so small. I''ve noticed your other entries have also been under the 800px max. In addition to  littlemav''s advice, here''s a tutorial that may help. Using Photoshop to Prepare Photos for DPC Challenges', '2014-06-25 15:26:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(7233370, 1118230, 158219, '<td valign="top">Beautimus shot Janine!</td>', 'Beautimus shot Janine!', '2014-06-25 19:03:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(7233371, 1117961, 83149, '<td valign="top">Pretty impressive to get such a sharp interior for a 10 second shot.  Nice job.</td>', 'Pretty impressive to get such a sharp interior for a 10 second shot.  Nice job.', '2014-06-25 19:14:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(7233375, 1117906, 83149, '<td valign="top">Glad I could inspire you (at least I think it was me)!  <br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1117117" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1939/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1117117.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1939/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1117117.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1939/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1117117.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>I used to drive past this bridge every night for over 10 years, and I kept saying to myself, if they ever have all the lights working, I am going to have to get a picture.  It was a long wait, but I got a <a href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/thecolliers/sets/72157621894131573" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">few good shots</a> that night.  It is a very scenic spot, day or night.<br/> <br/>I figured this was your''s when I saw it.</td>', 'Glad I could inspire you (at least I think it was me)!     I used to drive past this bridge every night for over 10 years, and I kept saying to myself, if they ever have all the lights working, I am going to have to get a picture.  It was a long wait, but I got a few good shots that night.  It is a very scenic spot, day or night. I figured this was your''s when I saw it.', '2014-06-25 19:31:32.000000', NULL, 0),
